%S A399987 1,1,1,1,2,11,79,633,5700,57027,625021,7440523
%N A399987 The number of distinct 4-inversion sets in the symmetric group on n elements.  A 4-inversion for a permutation w is a set of 4 values appearing in decreasing order in the one-line notation for w.
%D A399987 Sara Billey, Herman Chau, and Kevin Liu, <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2610.31795">Affine Higher Bruhat Orders</a>, arXiv:2610.31795 [math.CO], Oct. 22, 2026.
%e A399987 The permutation w=[5,3,4,2,1] has one 4-inverison {[1,2,4,5]}.
%Y A399987 Column k=4 of A399980.
%K A399987 nonn,more,new
%O A399987 0,5
